    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHey there, hope you are well! I have just started to use `mini.files` and love the concept so far. In my opinion, it combines `Oil` and `nvim-tree` very well!\r\n\r\nOne thing I found is in Windows,  mini.files won't be able to send files from `D:\\` to `stdpath('data')` which is located in `C:\\` when  `permanent_delete=false` is set. This could be due to system limitation but like to check in case this can be fixed with some workaround. \r\n\r\nI have just tested, moving files using `!mv` from Command Mode from `D:\\` to `C:\\` is working fine. \r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.10.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n0. Config `permanent_delete = false`\r\n1. Assuming `stdpath('data')` in drive C, cd to `d:\\` using Nvim Command mode\r\n2. Open mini.files and delete any file and then sync \r\n3. File will be back (without removing / moving)\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nFile to be moved to the desiganted dir. \r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nFile is never moved. Buffer is updated with the file been added back",
