            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis sounds plausible, but I can not reproduce because I don't have proper access to Windows machine to confirm myself.\r\n\r\nIt seems to be a fundamental limitation of chosen 'mini.files' approach to not permanent delete, because moving files across different partition [seems to be not supported by `vim.loop.fs_rename()`](https://github.com/nodejs/node-v0.x-archive/issues/2703). This will also manifest itself in that regular moving files across disks/partitions doesn't work. Could you, please, confirm that also?\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nThere are several solutions to this:\r\n- Implement own move function which recursively copies to the destination and then deletes the original. I didn't really want to do this because it might not play nicely with file metadata (like when it was created, modified, etc.). But this will also make regular move work across partitions.\r\n- Create separate \"trash\" directory on every partition/volume so that not persistent delete works.\r\n\r\nI'll think about it.",
