            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I totally forgot that recursive copy is already implemented as 'mini.files' helper. So making moving across devices work was [quite a concise change](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/commit/ce55a9fe9853c12162f16176a3c16d7b4e5c59b3#diff-3887c91f311fab10378f1a9cfa5f36a4b04f9efd4429fccacbb8632201831da5). If it mattered only for moving files, I'd probably won't add this, but this case of \"move to trash from different volume\" tips the scale.\r\n\r\nThis should now be resolved on latest `main`. Thanks again for pointing this out!\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nAlso (as a drive-by improvement), the \"delete\" action description now depends on whether it is permanent or not (\"DELETE\" vs \"MOVE TO TRASH\"). This should add an extra layer of visual feedback that files won't get permanently deleted.",
