        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Also (as a drive-by improvement), the \"delete\" action description now depends on whether it is permanent or not (\"DELETE\" vs \"MOVE TO TRASH\"). This should add an extra layer of visual feedback that files won't get permanently deleted.\r\n\r\nJust a follow up for completeness. There are now [many changes](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#minifiles) in how confirmation lines are computed. This also includes another change to how delete is shown: always with \"DELETE\" description but entry name followed by either \"(permanently)\" or \"(to trash)\". I reconsidered this because the new way is more aligned with how create action is shown.",
            "created_at": "2024-08-23T16:08:46Z",
